---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-04-founders-phone-required.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-04',
  title: 'Founders application requires a phone number again',
  tags: ['waitlist', 'lead-capture', 'founders', 'sms'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 4, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    The Founders application at
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> requires a
    phone number from every applicant, whatever their preferred way to be reached. This replaces
    the October 3 change that made the number optional unless a call or a text was requested.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Every applicant books a tour, and we need a way to reach each of them about it. Giving a
      number is not agreement to be texted: the text message consent box stays separate,
      unticked and optional, with the same wording and version as before.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">How it works</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The Phone / WhatsApp field carries the required asterisk, and its Optional tag is gone. Its
      helper text now reads "So we can reach you about your tour. We default to US format; start
      with + and your country code for international." Submitting without a number shows an
      inline message and focuses the field, and <code>/api/contact</code> refuses a Founders
      application with no number. Every number is still checked as a real phone number. The
      Best Way To Reach You choice stays, since it still says how the applicant prefers to be
      contacted. Other forms that post to <code>/api/contact</code> keep the phone optional.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
